  "notes": [
    "A vertical scan streak runs through the last digit of every Date Granted on both pages, so the year is recorded as \"2?\" where that digit is cut (e.g. \"Jan-2?\"). For most rows the remnant looks like the \"6\" of 2026 (the Q1 2026 report dates the same debtors Jan-26/Feb-26/Mar-26), but the remnants for \"Abalos, Junard\" (May) and \"Torre, Crisostomo Jr.\" (Jul) are shaped differently (possibly 2025). Dates were not guessed; the paths are listed in unreadable.",
    "Each item row has its balance repeated in one aging column (two rows also show a stray \"-\" under 91-365 days, kept as 0). A row on page 2 below \"Yrastorza, Raphael, Sr.\" shows only \"-\" in Amount Balance and \"Travel\" and is not transcribed. All column totals equal the sum of the rows. Certification names marked SIGNED by hand.",
    "As in Q1 2026, very old balances from the 2019-2020 reports (e.g. Abugan, Cleto 8,376.00; Gako, Ireneo 3,996.00; Gato, Juan 1,900.00; Javier, Rommel 1,950.00; Roble, Paz 1,730.00) now carry recent dates and sit under \"31-90 days\"."
  ],
